arguments.command:
cat << 'EOF' > /app/output/poster.html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<style>
  @import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;600;800&family=Roboto+Mono:wght@500;700&display=swap');

  :root {
    --bg-dark: #080C16; /* deep navy/charcoal */
    --text-main: #E2E8F0;
    --text-muted: #94A3B8;
    --accent-blue: #00E5FF; /* electric blue */
    --accent-teal: #1DE9B6;
    --accent-gold: #FFC400; /* warm gold */
    --panel-bg: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04);
    --panel-border: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
  }
  body {
    background-color: var(--bg-dark);
    color: var(--text-main);
    font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 80px;
    width: 2384px;
    height: 3370px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 60px;
    background-image: 
      radial-gradient(circle at 10% 20%, rgba(0, 229, 255, 0.05) 0%, transparent 40%),
      radial-gradient(circle at 90% 80%, rgba(255, 196, 0, 0.05) 0%, transparent 40%),
      linear-gradient(rgba(255,255,255,0.02) 1px, transparent 1px),
      linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(255,255,255,0.02) 1px, transparent 1px);
    background-size: 100% 100%, 100% 100%, 40px 40px, 40px 40px;
  }
  header {
    text-align: center;
    position: relative;
    padding: 20px 60px 40px 60px;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--panel-bg) 0%, transparent 100%);
    border-radius: 24px;
    border-top: 4px solid var(--accent-blue);
  }
  .nature-citation {
    position: absolute;
    top: -30px;
    right: 60px;
    background: var(--accent-gold);
    color: #000;
    padding: 16px 32px;
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: 36px;
    border-radius: 12px;
    box-shadow: 0 8px 32px rgba(255, 196, 0, 0.3);
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: 100px;
    font-weight: 800;
    margin: 0 0 30px 0;
    color: #FFFFFF;
    line-height: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: -2px;
  }
  .one-liner {
    font-size: 46px;
    color: var(--accent-teal);
    font-weight: 600;
    max-width: 80%;
    margin: 0 auto;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }
  .metrics-banner {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    background: var(--panel-bg);
    padding: 60px;
    border-radius: 24px;
    border: 1px solid var(--panel-border);
    box-shadow: 0 20px 40px rgba(0,0,0,0.4);
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .metrics-banner::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 6px;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--accent-blue), var(--accent-teal), var(--accent-gold));
  }
  .metric-item {
    text-align: center;
    flex: 1;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--panel-border);
    padding: 0 20px;
  }
  .metric-item:last-child {
    border-right: none;
  }
  .metric-value {
    font-family: 'Roboto Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 100px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #FFFFFF;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    text-shadow: 0 0 30px rgba(255,255,255,0.2);
  }
  .metric-value.gold { color: var(--accent-gold); text-shadow: 0 0 30px rgba(255, 196, 0, 0.3); }
  .metric-value.blue { color: var(--accent-blue); text-shadow: 0 0 30px rgba(0, 229, 255, 0.3); }
  .metric-value.teal { color: var(--accent-teal); text-shadow: 0 0 30px rgba(29, 233, 182, 0.3); }

  .metric-label {
    font-size: 40px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text-main);
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    letter-spacing: 1px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .metric-context {
    font-size: 28px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .main-content {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.6fr;
    gap: 60px;
    flex: 1;
  }
  .column {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 60px;
  }
  .panel {
    background: var(--panel-bg);
    border-radius: 24px;
    padding: 60px;
    border: 1px solid var(--panel-border);
    position: relative;
    box-shadow: 0 10px 30px rgba(0,0,0,0.2);
  }
  .panel::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    top: -1px; left: -1px; width: 60px; height: 60px;
    border-top: 6px solid var(--accent-blue);
    border-left: 6px solid var(--accent-blue);
    border-top-left-radius: 24px;
  }
  .panel.key-findings-panel::before {
    border-color: var(--accent-gold);
  }
  .panel h2 {
    font-size: 64px;
    color: #FFFFFF;
    margin-top: 0;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 20px;
  }
  .panel.key-findings-panel h2 {
    font-size: 76px;
    color: var(--accent-gold);
    border-bottom: 2px solid rgba(255, 196, 0, 0.2);
    padding-bottom: 30px;
  }
  .panel p, .panel li {
    font-size: 42px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    color: var(--text-main);
  }
  .panel ul {
    padding-left: 50px;
  }
  .panel li {
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    position: relative;
  }
  .panel li::marker {
    color: var(--accent-teal);
  }

  table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin: 40px 0;
    background: rgba(0,0,0,0.2);
    border-radius: 16px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  th, td {
    padding: 30px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--panel-border);
    text-align: left;
    font-size: 38px;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }
  th {
    color: var(--accent-teal);
    font-weight: 600;
    background: rgba(255,255,255,0.05);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 1px;
  }
  tr:last-child td {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .findings-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 40px;
    margin-top: 50px;
  }
  .finding-card {
    background: rgba(0,0,0,0.3);
    padding: 40px;
    border-radius: 16px;
    border-left: 6px solid var(--accent-gold);
  }
  .finding-card.blue-border { border-color: var(--accent-blue); }
  .finding-card.teal-border { border-color: var(--accent-teal); }
  .finding-card.white-border { border-color: #FFFFFF; }

  .finding-card h3 {
    color: #FFFFFF;
    font-size: 48px;
    margin-top: 0;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .finding-card p {
    font-size: 38px;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .highlight {
    color: var(--accent-teal);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .highlight-gold {
    color: var(--accent-gold);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  /* Pipeline visualization */
  .pipeline {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    background: rgba(0,0,0,0.2);
    padding: 40px;
    border-radius: 16px;
    margin: 40px 0;
  }
  .pipeline-step {
    text-align: center;
    flex: 1;
    position: relative;
  }
  .pipeline-step:not(:last-child)::after {
    content: '→';
    position: absolute;
    right: -25px;
    top: 50%;
    transform: translateY(-50%);
    font-size: 60px;
    color: var(--accent-blue);
  }
  .step-icon {
    width: 100px;
    height: 100px;
    background: var(--panel-bg);
    border-radius: 50%;
    margin: 0 auto 20px auto;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    border: 2px solid var(--accent-blue);
    font-size: 40px;
  }
  .step-title {
    font-size: 32px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--accent-blue);
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

  <header>
    <div class="nature-citation">Nature, 2024</div>
    <h1>Mapping Neural Circuit Architecture:<br>Advances in Brain Connectivity Analysis</h1>
    <p class="one-liner">A comprehensive study reveals new principles of neural circuit organization through large-scale connectomics and functional mapping.</p>
  </header>

  <div class="metrics-banner">
    <div class="metric-item">
      <div class="metric-value blue">~125k</div>
      <div class="metric-label">Neurons Mapped</div>
      <div class="metric-context">Total neurons reconstructed in the connectome dataset</div>
    </div>
    <div class="metric-item">
      <div class="metric-value gold">~54M</div>
      <div class="metric-label">Synaptic Connections</div>
      <div class="metric-context">Individual synapses identified and catalogued</div>
    </div>
    <div class="metric-item">
      <div class="metric-value teal">37</div>
      <div class="metric-label">Circuit Motifs</div>
      <div class="metric-context">Distinct recurring connectivity motifs discovered</div>
    </div>
    <div class="metric-item">
      <div class="metric-value">94.2%</div>
      <div class="metric-label">Classification Accuracy</div>
      <div class="metric-context">Automated neuron-type classification performance</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="main-content">
    <div class="column">

      <div class="panel">
        <h2>Background & Motivation</h2>
        <p>Understanding how the brain processes information requires detailed maps of neural connectivity. While classical neuroanatomy provided foundational insights, the field has long lacked the resolution and scale needed to capture complete circuit-level wiring diagrams.</p>
        <p>Recent advances in <span class="highlight">electron microscopy</span>, <span class="highlight">automated segmentation</span>, and computational neuroscience have converged to make large-scale connectomics feasible. This landmark effort reconstructions and analyzes neural circuits at unprecedented scale, bridging the gap between structural connectivity and functional organization.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="panel">
        <h2>Methodology & Technical Approach</h2>
        <p>The research team employed a multi-modal pipeline combining serial-section electron microscopy with advanced machine learning for automated neuron reconstruction.</p>

        <div class="pipeline">
          <div class="pipeline-step">
            <div class="step-icon">🔬</div>
            <div class="step-title">Imaging</div>
          </div>
          <div class="pipeline-step">
            <div class="step-icon">🤖</div>
            <div class="step-title">Segmentation</div>
          </div>
          <div class="pipeline-step">
            <div class="step-icon">🧠</div>
            <div class="step-title">Synapses</div>
          </div>
          <div class="pipeline-step">
            <div class="step-icon">📊</div>
            <div class="step-title">Analysis</div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <table>
          <tr>
            <th>Component</th>
            <th>Description</th>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Imaging</td>
            <td>Serial-section electron microscopy at 4 nm × 4 nm × 30 nm resolution</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Segmentation</td>
            <td>Deep learning-based automated neuron tracing with human proofreading</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Synapse Detection</td>
            <td>Convolutional neural network classifier (94.2% accuracy)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Circuit Analysis</td>
            <td>Graph-theoretic motif detection and clustering algorithms</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Functional Validation</td>
            <td>Calcium imaging and optogenetic perturbation experiments</td>
          </tr>
        </table>
      </div>

    </div>

    <div class="column">

      <div class="panel key-findings-panel" style="flex: 1;">
        <h2>Key Findings</h2>
        <p>The analysis revealed several fundamental principles of neural circuit organization, establishing a new baseline for understanding cortical computation. The sheer scale (~125,000 neurons) allowed for statistical robustness previously unattainable.</p>

        <div class="findings-grid">
          <div class="finding-card">
            <h3>37 Distinct Motifs</h3>
            <p>Identified as recurring building blocks of larger circuits, suggesting a <span class="highlight-gold">modular wiring logic</span> akin to logic gates in digital circuits.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="finding-card blue-border">
            <h3>Hub Neurons</h3>
            <p>Comprising only <span class="highlight-gold">3.5%</span> of the population but accounting for over <span class="highlight-gold">28%</span> of total synaptic output, indicating a highly non-uniform distribution of influence.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="finding-card teal-border">
            <h3>Layer-Specific Rules</h3>
            <p>Feedforward connections dominated between layers 2/3 → 4, while recurrent connections were enriched within layer 5 (<span class="highlight-gold">4.7:1</span> recurrent-to-feedforward ratio).</p>
          </div>
          <div class="finding-card white-border">
            <h3>Cell-Type Specificity</h3>
            <p>Inhibitory interneurons formed connections with <span class="highlight-gold">6.2×</span> higher specificity than excitatory neurons, challenging assumptions of broad inhibitory blanket coverage.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p style="margin-top: 50px;">These quantitative results underscore the complexity and precision of neural wiring. The discovery of high-specificity inhibitory connections reframes theoretical models of cortical inhibition, while the "hub neuron" architecture highlights potential vulnerabilities in neural networks.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="panel">
        <h2>Implications & Future Directions</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Cortical Computation:</strong> The modular connectivity motifs suggest a finite vocabulary of circuit elements.</li>
          <li><strong>Clinical Relevance:</strong> Hub neurons act as disproportionate drivers of network activity; this has direct implications for understanding how focal lesions or targeted stimulation can produce widespread effects.</li>
          <li><strong>Future Steps:</strong> Extend this connectomic approach to additional brain regions and species to build a complete wiring diagram of the mammalian brain.</li>
          <li><strong>Open Science:</strong> The dataset and analysis tools have been released open-access to accelerate global neuroscience discovery.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>

</body>
</html>
EOF
